A||||4||fldevel||Whats the difference between all the fieros ???||||5||
Z||000000||fldevel||06-22-2000||09:05 PM||||this sounds stupid but im really curious ...<BR> what the diff between a <BR>  1. 2m4 and SE <BR>  2. 2m6 and GT <BR>  3. formula and exc...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||06-22-2000||09:24 PM||||2m4's are 4 cylinder Fieros<BR>2m6's are 6 cylinder Fieros... both these designations were used on 84, 85 and 86 Fieros, and dropped after that.  <P>SE's have higher levels of equipment... I'm not exactly sure what packages became standard.  I think they also had the aero front and rear fascia's like the 84 Indy and 85 GT.  Some SE's also had V6's.  I don't think the aero was used on 84 SE's.  I am sure someone with an SE can help you out more with them.<P>85 and early 86 GT's had the aero nose and tail on the notchback coupe body... 86.5-88 GT's were fastbacks.  All GT's had V6's.<P>For 88 the Formula model appeared... it had the GT V6 engine and WS6 suspension with the normal 87/88  coupe notchback body.<P>Hope this helps some.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||06-22-2000||09:36 PM||||Formula88 pretty much said it all. Se usually just had some suspension and misc. other mods...<BR>2m4= 2 seat, mid engine, 4 cylinder<BR>2m6= 2 seat, mid engine, 6 cylinder<BR>84-all 4 cylinders...Se option includes some suspension and misc. differences. Non aero body (except for Indy).<BR>85-pretty much the same...only 6 cylinder option available.<BR>86-same, only now has aero package.<BR>All Gt's had V6's and aero packages. 85 Gt was notchback, 86-88 were fastbacks.<BR>Se models dropped in 88 inlew of Formula.<BR>Formula had standard body w/Gt performance.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||06-22-2000||09:50 PM||||One, possibly two minor corrections to Fformula's post. The 85 SE models did not have the aero nose, I know because I have one. But, the 86-87 SE models do have the aero nose, so you were right about that part. Also, there are rumors of a few 86 notchback GTs being made, but to my knowledge, there has never been one documented. The 86.5 model year designation was when the 4 speed was dropped from the GT line up and was replaced by the Getrag 5 speed, which was midway through the 1986 model year. If anyone has a real 86 notchback GT, I'd like to see the VIN, it just might be one of the rarest Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||06-22-2000||11:50 PM||||batboy, it never existed.  To the guy who started this, buy a Fiero Spotters guide, its like 5 bucks and you will use it a lot.  Email mark Corbin, can't remember his email but maybe someone can post it for me.<BR>||||reg||12
